Hi Dakota,
I followed your workflow and was not able to reproduce the error (I've attached a sample RMD I was able to generate). I will flag Gonzalo to take a look at the error when he is back from vacation.
In the meantime try updating the 'knitr' package. Also, if you are interested, you can also try updating to Wallace v2 and see if that version also gives you issues downloading the session code. It's a developmental version, but you should be able to run your workflow without issues. You can find instructions on how to install here <https://wallaceecomod.github.io/wallace/articles/tutorial-v2.html#setup>. The only difference is you will need to edit the csv of your occurrence data; the column header 'name' will need to be changed to 'scientific_name' to work properly.

-Bethany
PS: Just to put a face to the Wallace account, we met at the sky island panel discussion at ASM

